.\" SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT OR Apache-2.0
.TH RCMAKE 1 "2026-11-26" "rcmake 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
rcmake \- native Rust CMake 4.5.1 compatible build system driver
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B rcmake
.RI [ options ]
.B \-S
.I path-to-source
.B \-B
.I path-to-build
.br
.B rcmake
.RI [ options ]
.I path-to-source
|
.I path-to-existing-build
.br
.B rcmake \-\-build
.I dir
.RI [ options ]
.RB [ \-\-
.RI [ native-options ]]
.br
.B rcmake \-\-install
.I dir
.RI [ options ]
.br
.B rcmake \-\-workflow
.I options
.br
.B rcmake explain
.I name
.RB [ \-B
.IR build-dir ]
.RB [ \-\-target | \-\-var ]
.RB [ \-\-config
.IR cfg ]
.RB [ \-\-filter
.IR val ]
.RB [ \-\-json ]
.RB [ \-\-verbose ]
.RB [ \-\-color=auto|always|never ]
.br
.B rcmake \-P
.I script.cmake
.RB [ \-\-
.RI [ args... ]]
.br
.B rcmake \-E
.I command
.RI [ args... ]
.br
.B rcmake ctest
.RI [ options ]
.br
.B rcmake cpack
.RI [ options ]
.br
.B rcmake lsp
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B rcmake
is a from-scratch replacement for CMake 4.5.1 written in safe Rust.
A single multi-call binary implements
.BR cmake ,
.BR ctest ,
.BR cpack ,
and the Language Server Protocol (LSP) server (invoked via the
.B rcmake-lsp
symlink or
.BR "rcmake lsp" ),
reading the same
.IR CMakeLists.txt ,
presets, and
.I CMakeCache.txt
files as CMake 4.5.1 and writing compatible build trees.
.SS Execution modes
The executable selects its command-line surface from
.BR argv[0] :
.TP
.B Native mode (\fBrcmake\fP)
Enables the persistent compiler probe cache, incremental configure replay,
the
.B explain
subcommand, rich diagnostics, configure profiling, hermetic input checks,
and FetchContent lockfile enforcement.
.TP
.B Compatibility mode (\fBcmake\fP, \fBctest\fP, \fBcpack\fP)
Matches CMake 4.5.1 command-line flags, diagnostic formatting, and exit codes.
Native extension flags are rejected as unknown options in compatibility mode.
Setting
.B RCMAKE_ORACLE_MODE=1
forces compatibility mode even when invoked as
.BR rcmake .
.SH NATIVE EXTENSIONS
These subcommands and flags are accepted only in native
.B rcmake
mode (rejected in compatibility mode).
Configure-only flags such as
.BR \-\-profile ,
.BR \-\-hermetic ,
.BR \-\-fetch-lock ,
and
.B \-\-no-probe-cache
apply during project configure, while
.B \-\-diagnostics=cmake|rich
(and default TTY rich errors) also apply in native
.B rcmake \-P
script mode; compatibility
.B cmake \-P
always stays in CMake diagnostic format.
.SS Explain subcommand
.TP
.BI "rcmake explain " name
Inspect a configured build directory and explain where target
.I name
gets its compile flags, definitions, include directories, and link libraries,
or where variable
.I name
gets its effective value and cache provenance.
.RS
.TP
.BI \-B " build-dir"
Read
.I CMakeCache.txt
from
.IR build-dir .
Defaults to the current working directory.
.TP
.B \-\-target
Look up a target or alias.
.TP
.B \-\-var
Look up a variable.
Mutually exclusive with
.BR \-\-target ,
.BR \-\-config ,
and
.BR \-\-filter .
.TP
.BI \-\-config " cfg"
Select a target build configuration (for example
.B Debug
or
.BR Release ).
Implies
.BR \-\-target .
.TP
.BI \-\-filter " val"
Select a matching target value or compiler flag (for example
.BR \-O2
or
.BR \-DFOO=1 ).
Implies
.BR \-\-target .
.TP
.B \-\-json
Emit one JSON report (`rcmake-explain-v1`) to standard output.
.TP
.B \-\-verbose
Show full values and call stacks in terminal output.
.TP
.BR \-\-color=auto | always | never
Control ANSI color output.
The default is
.BR auto .
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show
.B rcmake explain
usage and exit.
.RE
.SS Native configure options
Native extension flags take their value with an equals sign in the same
argument.
.TP
.BR \-\-diagnostics=cmake | rich
Select diagnostic formatting.
.B cmake
matches upstream CMake 4.5.1 text.
.B rich
renders source excerpts, spans, and suggested fixes.
When omitted in native mode,
.B rcmake
checks
.B RCMAKE_DIAGNOSTICS
and otherwise selects
.B rich
when standard error is a terminal and
.B cmake
when standard error is redirected.
Compatibility mode always uses
.BR cmake .
.TP
.BR \-\-profile [ =\fIdir\fP ]
Record configure timing and write
.IR trace.json ,
.IR stacks.folded ,
and an interactive
.I flamegraph.html
under
.IR dir .
When
.I dir
is omitted, output goes to
.I rcmake-profile
inside the build directory.
.TP
.BR \-\-hermetic [ =warn | strict ]
Audit undeclared configure inputs including environment variables, files outside
the source, build, and tool roots, subprocesses, and network access.
.B warn
(the default when no value is given) reports violations and continues.
.B strict
rejects undeclared inputs with a non-zero exit status.
Allowlists are configured via
.BR RCMAKE_HERMETIC_ALLOW_ENV ,
.BR RCMAKE_HERMETIC_ALLOW_PATHS ,
and
.BR RCMAKE_HERMETIC_ALLOW_PROGRAMS .
.TP
.BR \-\-fetch-lock=off | auto | update | frozen
Control FetchContent lockfile verification and pinned source reuse.
.B off
disables lockfile checks.
.B auto
(default) verifies against an existing lockfile when present.
.B update
records resolved archive and Git pins into the lockfile.
.B frozen
requires every fetched dependency to match a verified pin and blocks unpinned
or unsupported transfers.
.TP
.B \-\-no-probe-cache
Disable the persistent compiler probe cache for this configure run.
To select a custom shared cache root or probe cache root, set
.B RCMAKE_CACHE_DIR
or
.B RCMAKE_PROBE_CACHE_DIR
in the environment.
.SH CONFIGURE OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-S " path-to-source"
Explicitly specify the source directory.
.TP
.BI \-B " path-to-build"
Explicitly specify the build directory.
.TP
.BI \-C " initial-cache"
Pre-load a script to populate the cache before configuring.
.TP
.BI \-D " var" "[:" type "]=" value
Create or update a CMake cache entry.
.TP
.BI \-U " globbing-expr"
Remove matching entries from the CMake cache.
.TP
.BI \-G " generator-name"
Select a build system generator.
Supported generators are
.BR "Unix Makefiles" ,
.BR Ninja ,
.BR "Ninja Multi-Config" ,
.B Xcode
(on macOS),
.B "Visual Studio 17 2022"
(on Windows), and
.B "Visual Studio 18 2026"
(on Windows).
.TP
.BI \-T " toolset-name"
Specify the generator toolset where supported.
.TP
.BI \-A " platform-name"
Specify the generator platform where supported.
.TP
.BI \-\-toolchain " file"
Specify a toolchain file
.RB ( CMAKE_TOOLCHAIN_FILE ).
.TP
.BI \-\-install-prefix " dir"
Specify the installation prefix
.RB ( CMAKE_INSTALL_PREFIX ).
.TP
.BI \-\-project-file " name"
Specify an alternate top-level project listfile name.
.TP
.BI \-\-preset " name"
Use a configure preset from
.I CMakePresets.json
or
.IR CMakeUserPresets.json .
.TP
.BI \-\-presets-file " file"
Read presets from a specific file.
.TP
.BR \-\-list-presets [ =\fItype\fP ]
List available or defined presets.
Valid types are
.BR configure ,
.BR build ,
.BR test ,
.BR package ,
.BR workflow ,
.BR all ,
.BR defined ,
and any type suffixed with
.BR \-defined .
.TP
.B \-\-fresh
Remove any existing cache file before configuring.
.TP
.BI \-W category "\fR, \fP" \-Wno- category "\fR, \fP" \-Werror= category "\fR, \fP" \-Wno-error= category
Enable, suppress, or promote diagnostic warning categories
.RB ( dev ,
.BR author ,
.BR deprecated ,
.BR policy ,
.BR strict ,
.BR experimental ,
.BR non-target-directive ,
.BR install-absolute-destination ,
.BR uninitialized ,
.BR unused-cli ).
.TP
.BR \-\-warn-uninitialized ", " \-\-no-warn-unused-cli ", " \-\-check-system-vars
Control uninitialized variable, unused CLI variable, and system file checks.
.TP
.BR \-\-compile-no-warning-as-error ", " \-\-link-no-warning-as-error
Ignore
.B COMPILE_WARNING_AS_ERROR
or
.B LINK_WARNING_AS_ERROR
properties and variables.
.TP
.BR \-\-log-level= ERROR|WARNING|NOTICE|STATUS|VERBOSE|DEBUG|TRACE
Set message verbosity.
.B \-\-log-context
prepends message context.
.TP
.BR \-\-trace ", " \-\-trace-expand ", " \-\-trace-format=human|json-v1 ", " \-\-trace-source=\fIfile\fP ", " \-\-trace-redirect=\fIfile\fP
Enable CMake script tracing and control trace output.
.TP
.BR \-\-debug-output ", " \-\-debug-trycompile ", " \-\-debug-find ", " \-\-debug-find-pkg=\fIpkgs\fP ", " \-\-debug-find-var=\fIvars\fP
Enable configure and find-command debug diagnostics.
.TP
.BI \-\-sarif-output= file
Write SARIF 2.1.0 diagnostic output to
.IR file .
.TP
.BI \-\-graphviz= file
Generate a Graphviz dependency graph.
.TP
.BR \-\-profiling-format=google-trace ", " \-\-profiling-output=\fIfile\fP
Write CMake-format Google Trace profiling JSON.
.TP
.BR \-L [ A ][ H ] ", " \-LR [ A ][ H ] " " \fIregex\fP
List cached variables, optionally including advanced entries, help strings,
or regex filtering.
.TP
.BR \-N ", " \-P " " \fIfile\fP ", " \-E " " \fIcmd\fP ", " \-\-find-package ", " \-\-system-information " [" \fIfile\fP "], " \-\-print-config-dir
View mode, script mode, cross-platform command mode, legacy find-package mode,
system information dump, and user File API config directory lookup.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-H ", " \-\-help ", " \-\-version [ =json-v1 ] ", " \-\-help-*
Print usage, version information, or bundled CMake 4.5.1 reference topics
.RB ( \-\-help-command ,
.BR \-\-help-diagnostic ,
.BR \-\-help-manual ,
.BR \-\-help-module ,
.BR \-\-help-policy ,
.BR \-\-help-property ,
.BR \-\-help-variable ,
and their
.B \-list
variants).
.SH BUILD, INSTALL, AND WORKFLOW MODES
.TP
.BI "\-\-build " dir
Build a generated project tree.
Accepts
.BR \-\-preset ,
.BR \-\-presets-file ,
.BR \-\-list-presets [ =defined ],
.BR \-j / \-\-parallel
.RI [ jobs ],
.BR \-t / \-\-target
.IR tgt ,
.BR \-\-config
.IR cfg ,
.BR \-\-clean-first ,
.BR \-\-resolve-package-references=on|only|off ,
.BR \-v / \-\-verbose ,
and
.B \-\-
followed by native build tool arguments.
.TP
.BI "\-\-install " dir
Install a generated project tree.
Accepts
.BR \-\-config
.IR cfg ,
.BR \-\-component
.IR comp ,
.BR \-\-default-directory-permissions
.IR perm ,
.BR \-j / \-\-parallel
.IR jobs ,
.BR \-\-prefix
.IR dir ,
.BR \-\-strip ,
and
.BR \-v / \-\-verbose .
.TP
.B \-\-workflow
Execute a workflow preset's configure, build, test, and package steps.
Accepts
.BR \-\-preset ,
.BR \-\-presets-file ,
.BR \-\-list-presets [ =defined ],
and
.BR \-\-fresh .
.SH COMPANION TOOLS
.SS ctest
When invoked through a
.B ctest
link (compatibility mode) or as
.BR "rcmake ctest" ,
the binary runs CMake test suites with support for
parallel scheduling, fixtures, resource specifications, labels, repeat modes,
JUnit XML, dashboard submission, and
.B \-S
scripts.
Common options include
.BR \-\-test-dir
.IR dir ,
.BR \-C
.IR cfg ,
.BR \-R
.I regex
(include tests),
.BR \-E
.I regex
(exclude tests),
.BR \-L
.I regex
(include labels),
.BR \-LE
.I regex
(exclude labels),
.BR \-j / \-\-parallel
.RI [ jobs ],
.BR \-\-output-on-failure ,
.BR \-\-output-junit
.IR file ,
.BR \-\-preset
.IR name ,
.BR \-\-rerun-failed ,
.BR \-\-stop-on-failure ,
.BR \-\-repeat
.IR mode:n ,
.BR \-\-timeout
.IR secs ,
.BR \-N / \-\-show-only [ =human|json-v1|json-v1-raw ],
.BR \-V / \-VV / \-Q ,
and
.BR \-S
.IR script .
.SS cpack
When invoked through a
.B cpack
link (compatibility mode) or as
.BR "rcmake cpack" ,
the binary packages build artifacts using
.BR \-G
.I generators
.RB ( TGZ ,
.BR TXZ ,
.BR TZST ,
.BR TBZ2 ,
.BR TZ ,
.BR TAR ,
.BR STGZ ,
.BR ZIP ,
.BR 7Z ,
their compression variants, Linux
.B DEB
and
.BR RPM ,
.BR External ,
and macOS
.B Bundle
and
.BR DragNDrop ),
.BR \-C
.IR configs ,
.BR \-D
.IR var=value ,
.BR \-\-config
.IR file ,
.BR \-P
.IR name ,
.BR \-R
.IR version ,
.BR \-B
.IR dir ,
.BR \-\-vendor
.IR name ,
.BR \-\-preset
.IR name ,
.BR \-\-presets-file
.IR file ,
.BR \-\-list-presets ,
.BR \-V / \-\-verbose ,
.BR \-\-debug ,
.BR \-\-trace ,
and
.BR \-\-trace-expand .
.SS rcmake-lsp
Invoked through the
.B rcmake-lsp
symlink or as
.BR "rcmake lsp" ,
the same multi-call binary runs a Language Server Protocol server for
.I CMakeLists.txt
and
.I *.cmake
files communicating over standard input and standard output with JSON-RPC
.B Content-Length
framing (accepting
.B \-\-help
and
.BR \-\-version ).
It provides hover, completion, go to definition, document symbols, semantic
tokens, diagnostics, quick fixes, and formatting.
When built with the
.B eval,stdio
features (the default in release archives), hover evaluates variables, targets,
and generator expressions in memory without spawning external processes.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
Command-line options take precedence over environment variables.
Native speed and diagnostic variables apply only in native
.B rcmake
mode.
.SS Mode and output
.TP
.B RCMAKE_ORACLE_MODE
Set to
.B 1
to force compatibility mode even when invoked as
.BR rcmake .
.TP
.B RCMAKE_DIAGNOSTICS
Set to
.B cmake
or
.B rich
in native mode.
Unset defaults to
.B rich
on a TTY standard error and
.B cmake
otherwise.
.TP
.BR NO_COLOR ", " CLICOLOR_FORCE
Disable ANSI color when
.B NO_COLOR
is set.
.B CLICOLOR_FORCE=1
forces ANSI color in rich mode and overrides
.BR NO_COLOR .
.TP
.B RCMAKE_PROFILE
Set the native configure profile output directory.
.TP
.B RCMAKE_EXEC_LOG
Write JSON Lines invocation records (including
.B tool
and effective
.B persona
fields) to this path.
.TP
.B RCMAKE_VENDORED_DATA_ROOT
Override the directory containing bundled CMake 4.5.1
.IR Modules/ ,
.IR Templates/ ,
and
.I Help/
files.
.SS Probe cache and incremental replay
.TP
.B RCMAKE_CACHE_DIR
Override the shared storage root for the compiler probe cache and FetchContent
cache.
.TP
.B RCMAKE_CACHE_MAX_SIZE
Set the shared store size limit in bytes (default 2 GiB).
.TP
.B RCMAKE_PROBE_CACHE
Select
.B readwrite
(default),
.BR readonly ,
.BR verify ,
or
.BR off .
.TP
.B RCMAKE_NO_PROBE_CACHE
Set to
.B 1
to disable the probe cache.
.TP
.B RCMAKE_PROBE_CACHE_DIR
Override the probe storage root separately from
.BR RCMAKE_CACHE_DIR .
.TP
.B RCMAKE_PROBE_JOBS
Positive integer number of concurrent probe jobs (default min(4, CPUs)).
.TP
.B RCMAKE_NO_INCREMENTAL
Set to
.B 1
to disable incremental configure replay.
.TP
.B RCMAKE_OFFLINE
Set to
.B 1
to disable remote probe cache access.
.TP
.BR RCMAKE_CACHE_REMOTE ", " RCMAKE_CACHE_REMOTE_AUTH ", " RCMAKE_CACHE_REMOTE_TOKEN ", " RCMAKE_CACHE_REMOTE_HEADER ", " RCMAKE_CACHE_REMOTE_WRITE
Configure an optional HTTPS remote probe cache
.RB ( anonymous ,
.BR bearer ,
.BR header ,
or
.B s3
authentication).
.SS FetchContent lockfile and hermetic checks
.TP
.B RCMAKE_FETCH_LOCK
Select
.B auto
(default),
.BR off ,
.BR update ,
or
.BR frozen .
.TP
.B RCMAKE_FETCH_LOCK_FILE
Override the lockfile path (default
.I rcmake-fetch.lock
in the source directory).
.TP
.B RCMAKE_FETCH_OFFLINE
Set to
.B 1
to disable network transfers for FetchContent and ExternalProject.
.TP
.BR RCMAKE_FETCH_PREFETCH ", " RCMAKE_FETCH_JOBS ", " RCMAKE_FETCH_GIT_READ_ONLY ", " RCMAKE_FETCH_GIT_MAX_SIZE
Control parallel FetchContent prefetching and Git mirror cache limits.
.TP
.B RCMAKE_HERMETIC
Select
.B off
(default),
.BR warn ,
or
.BR strict .
.TP
.BR RCMAKE_HERMETIC_ALLOW_ENV ", " RCMAKE_HERMETIC_ALLOW_PATHS ", " RCMAKE_HERMETIC_ALLOW_PROGRAMS
Semicolon-separated allowlists of environment variable names, absolute
directory or file paths, and absolute executable paths permitted in hermetic
mode.
.SS Standard CMake and CTest variables
.TP
.BR CMAKE_GENERATOR ", " CMAKE_BUILD_PARALLEL_LEVEL ", " CMAKE_INSTALL_PARALLEL_LEVEL ", " CTEST_PARALLEL_LEVEL ", " CTEST_OUTPUT_ON_FAILURE
Standard CMake and CTest defaults honored by
.BR rcmake ,
.BR cmake ,
and
.BR ctest .
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The command succeeded.
For
.BR "rcmake explain" ,
the requested target or variable was found.
.TP
.B 1
Configure, generation, build, install, test, packaging, or
.B explain
query failed (including not-found or ambiguous
.B explain
names).
.TP
.B 2
Invalid arguments to
.B rcmake explain
or an unavailable configured build directory.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I <prefix>/share/cmake-4.5/
Bundled CMake 4.5.1 modules, templates, and compressed help reference installed
next to
.IR <prefix>/bin/rcmake .
.TP
.I CMakeCache.txt
Generated build-tree cache read by
.B rcmake explain
and incremental reconfigures.
.TP
.IR CMakePresets.json ", " CMakeUserPresets.json
Project and user CMake Presets files (schema version 13).
.TP
.I rcmake-fetch.lock
Default FetchContent lockfile in the project source directory.
.TP
.I <build>/rcmake-profile/
Default output directory for
.B \-\-profile
containing
.IR trace.json ,
.IR stacks.folded ,
and
.IR flamegraph.html .
.TP
.I ~/Library/Caches/rcmake
Default cache directory on macOS.
On Linux the default is
.I $XDG_CACHE_HOME/rcmake
or
.IR ~/.cache/rcmake .
On Windows the default is
.IR %LOCALAPPDATA%\ercmake\ecache .
Overridden by
.BR RCMAKE_CACHE_DIR .
.SH EXAMPLES
Configure and build a project with Ninja:
.PP
.EX
rcmake -S . -B build -G Ninja
rcmake --build build
.EE
.PP
Explain where target
.B app
gets its
.B \-O2
flag:
.PP
.EX
rcmake explain app -B build --filter -O2
.EE
.PP
Profile a configure run and audit hermetic inputs:
.PP
.EX
rcmake -S . -B build -G Ninja --profile=prof --hermetic=strict
.EE
.PP
Update and then enforce a FetchContent lockfile:
.PP
.EX
rcmake -S . -B build --fetch-lock=update
rcmake -S . -B build --fetch-lock=frozen
.EE
.PP
Run tests via the compatibility alias:
.PP
.EX
ctest --test-dir build --output-on-failure -j
.EE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR cmake (1),
.BR ctest (1),
.BR cpack (1)
